================
Crystal fragment
================

. Ab initio calculations are performed on the fragment
  to obtain structure factors, charges, etc.

. The fragment need not be an asymmetric unit.

. Repeated atoms are assigned a 'repetition factor' which
  is used to scale the structure factor contribution from
  that atom. You can manually reset this.

. Only the unique atoms in the fragment have their
  positions and ADPs refined.

. The Z factor for the crystal is defined with respect to
  the no. of electrons in the fragment


No. of fragment atoms ........... 8
No. of unique fragment atoms .... 5
Z factor ........................ 2.000000

Density partition model ......... oc-hirshfeld
Is one-center TF model? ......... T


